# THE GATEHUB — Global Stability & Integration

Treat THE GATEHUB as **one application**, not isolated pages.

## Before building anything new

1. Search the codebase for similar features (player, editor, publish, preview, quiz, PDF, video, cards, forms).
2. **Reuse** existing components, hooks, services, APIs, layouts, and utilities.
3. **Extend** shared logic — never duplicate business rules.
4. Verify the change does not regress auth, routing, refresh, back/forward, dashboards, player, payments, progress, or permissions.

## Single sources of truth (prefer these)

| Concern | Use |
|--------|-----|
| Course player (student + instructor preview) | `CoursePlayerPage` + `buildInstructorCoursePreviewPath` |
| Uploaded video | `VideoPlayer` → `UploadedVideoPlayer` + `courseMediaUrls` |
| Notes PDF | `CoursePdfViewer` + `/api/lectures/:id/notes-pdf` |
| Media URLs | `resolveCourseMediaUrl`, `resolveLectureVideoUrl` |
| Preview return navigation | `instructorPreview.ts` |
| Cache after curriculum/notes/quiz edits | `invalidateCourseContentCaches()` |

## New content must work end-to-end

When instructors create or update courses, sections, lectures (video / notes / quiz / file), or captions:

- **Student view** and **instructor preview** must use the same player and APIs.
- Invalidate `course-learn` + `sections` caches after saves (via `invalidateCourseContentCaches`).
- Notes require `compiledPdfUrl` (compile + attach) before PDF shows in player.
- Upload videos need `videoType: "upload"` and relative `/uploads/...` URLs.
- Do not add parallel renderers (e.g. separate preview components) unless extending the shared one.

## UI / responsive

- No fixed widths that break mobile or ultrawide.
- Match existing typography, spacing, cards, buttons, and theme.
- Immersive content (video, notes) uses full viewport; sidebar toggles via shared pattern.

## Definition of done

Complete only when: existing features still work, new content appears in preview and student view without manual refresh tricks, no console/TS errors, and behavior matches the rest of the platform.
